diction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"latencyMs\":46688.62124999985}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"openai/o3","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"df1c85511e8bebdd":{"spanId":"df1c85511e8bebdd","traceId":"989d4d0ca4a2ca45ce8345e589f201c7","startTime":1753404042275,"endTime":1753404088965.411,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/o3\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Director-rank agent, the second-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Director-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Supervisor-rank agents, who themselves are fairly high-level actors who manage other agents. You are responsible for overseeing major operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to the Chief-rank agent, who is the highest authority in the firm.\\n\\nAs a #2 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Supervisor-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Director, all of your recruitments are Supervisor-rank agents. These are fairly high-level agents who will recruit other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" and middle managers down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\\n\\n---ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS FROM YOUR SUPERIOR---\\nYou will design the WordPress information architecture, choose plugins (login, membership, contact form), define user roles, and produce a deterministic plan for implementing pages and protected sections.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CMS_PLAN_V1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Motti (3) with sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1:\\\\n\\\\n]Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_PLAN_V1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CMS_PLAN_V1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"**Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – CMS_PLAN_V1**\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nA. HOSTING & BASELINE\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Hosting prerequisites (Infrastructure team)\\\\n   a. PHP ≥ 8.1, memory_limit ≥ 256 M, max_upload_filesize ≥ 32 M.\\\\n   b. MariaDB 10.5 / MySQL 8.0, InnoDB default.\\\\n   c. HTTPS enabled (Let’s Encrypt or other TLS cert) before public launch.\\\\n   d. Cron jobs allowed (for WP‐Cron replacement if traffic < 1k/day this can stay virtual).\\\\n   e. SMTP credentials or transactional-mail service (Postmark / SendGrid free tier) for registration emails.\\\\n   f. File-system write permissions for wp-content and install zip uploads.\\\\n\\\\n2. Fresh WordPress 6.5.x install in root directory; enforce automatic minor/major core updates:\\\\n   wp-config.php →\\\\n   define('WP_AUTO_UPDATE_CORE','minor');\\\\n\\\\n3. Theme baseline picked by Design director: “Twenty Twenty-Four” **or** “Astra Free”.\\\\n   • Must support: full-site-editing (FSE) hooks `header`, `footer`, `sidebar` if Astra.\\\\n   • Keep child-theme blank (style.css, functions.php) reserved for any CSS/JS overrides but *initially empty* to keep DEP deterministic.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nB. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE (IA)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nCreate pages in this exact slug order:\\\\n1. `/`  → “Home”\\\\n2. `/contact-us/` → “Contact Us”\\\\n3. `/bylaws/` → “HOA Bylaws” (public)\\\\n4. `/schools/` → “Nearby Schools” (public)\\\\n5. `/dues/` → “Dues” (PROTECTED)\\\\n6. `/annual-meetings/` → “Annual Meetings” (PROTECTED)\\\\n7. `/news-events/` → “News & Events” (PROTECTED)\\\\n\\\\nNavigation menu “Main Menu” created and assigned to Theme primary location using identical order.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nC. PLUGIN STACK (all free unless noted)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. User self-registration + manual admin approval + access-code field\\\\n   • Plugin: **“User Registration – Custom Registration Form, Login and User Profile”** by WP Everest.\\\\n     – Free tier supports manual approval, custom fields & form shortcodes.\\\\n\\\\n2. Content/membership protection\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Content Control – User Access Restriction”** by Code Atlantic (100 % free, no paywall).\\\\n\\\\n3. Simple page/block builder for non-technical updates\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Kadence Blocks – Gutenberg Blocks for Page Builder Features”** (free) – adds pre-made block patterns, accordions, tabs; stays inside core editor.\\\\n\\\\n4. Contact form with CAPTCHA\\\\n   • Plugin: **“WPForms Lite”** (free) – includes hCaptcha & reCAPTCHA v2/v3 support.\\\\n\\\\n5. PDF file management / embed & protection\\\\n   • Plugin: **“EmbedPress”** (free) – Gutenberg block to embed PDF inline.\\\\n   • **“Prevent Direct Access – PDA Lite”** (free) – protects PDFs so file URLs respect membership rules.\\\\n\\\\n6. Security hardening\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Limit Login Attempts Reloaded”** (free).\\\\n   • (Optional) “WP 2FA” free module if MFA desired later.\\\\n\\\\n7. Role/Capability management convenience\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Members”** by MemberPress (free) – create Custom Role “Resident”.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD. STEP-BY-STEP CONFIGURATION\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD1. Global order of operations (deterministic):\\\\n   1. Complete WP install (A2).\\\\n   2. Install theme (A3).\\\\n   3. Install *all* plugins in section C but keep them **deactivated**.\\\\n   4. Activate plugins sequentially in this exact order to avoid capability conflicts:\\\\n      a. Members\\\\n      b. User Registration\\\\n      c. Content Control\\\\n      d. Kadence Blocks\\\\n      e. WPForms Lite\\\\n      f. EmbedPress\\\\n      g. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite\\\\n      h. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\n   5. Create roles, forms, rules as below.\\\\n\\\\nD2. Members plugin – role definitions\\\\n   • Create custom role **Resident**.\\\\n     Capabilities: `read`, `edit_posts` = false, `upload_files` = false. (Leave all others unchecked.)\\\\n   • (Core) Keep Administrator, Editor defaults.\\\\n\\\\nD3. User Registration plugin – registration form\\\\n   1. Create new form “Resident Signup”.\\\\n   2. Add core fields: First Name, Last Name, Email (username), Password.\\\\n   3. Add custom Text field “Access Code”.\\\\n      – Field meta-key: `hoa_access_code`.\\\\n      – Field set as *required*.\\\\n   4. Enable *Manual Admin Approval* (Settings ▸ General ▸ User Login Option ▸ “Admin Approve”).\\\\n   5. Form setting ▸ *Enable email confirmation* = OFF (because approval already required).\\\\n   6. Place validation rule via form *Field Visibility & Logic*:\\\\n      – If `hoa_access_code` ≠ “NEIGHBOR2024” (example), display error “Invalid HOA code”.\\\\n   7. Save form; copy generated shortcode `[user_registration_form id=\\\\\\\"XX\\\\\\\"]`.\\\\n   8. Create WordPress page `/register/` titled “Resident Registration”, paste shortcode.\\\\n   9. In WP ▸ Settings ▸ General ▸ “Membership – Anyone can register” = **unchecked** (security).\\\\n\\\\nD4. Content Control – protection rules\\\\n   • Rule 1: Protect Pages `Dues`, `Annual Meetings`, `News & Events`.\\\\n     – Access condition: Logged-in users with role = Resident OR ≥ Editor.\\\\n     – Redirect on failure: `/register/` (or custom message page).\\\\n   • Rule 2: Protect Media Files category “Protected PDFs” (auto-created by PDA Lite) with same role condition.\\\\n\\\\nD5. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite – PDF handling\\\\n   1. Settings ▸ Permalink Type: “Encrypted URL” (default).\\\\n   2. Upload PDF → Media Library → toggle “Protect this file”.\\\\n   3. Copy shortcode `[pda_protected url=\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\" download=\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"]` and insert inside protected pages.\\\\n\\\\nD6. WPForms Lite – contact form\\\\n   1. Create form “HOA Contact”. Fields: Name, Email, Message.\\\\n   2. Settings ▸ Spam Protection → enable Google reCAPTCHA v3 (site key provided separately by Infrastructure).\\\\n   3. Notifications → send to `hoaboard@example.com`.\\\\n   4. Embed form in “Contact Us” page using Gutenberg block.\\\\n\\\\nD7. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\n   • Settings → Lockout at 4 retries, 30 min lockout, 24 h increase, GDPR consent banner OFF.\\\\n\\\\nD8. Kadence Blocks (non-technical editing enablement)\\\\n   • Install Starter Templates if Astra theme chosen; else use built-in patterns.\\\\n   • Provide training doc (outside DEP) listing: Accordion (meeting minutes), Info Box (dues summary), Gallery (events photos).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nE. SAMPLE WORKFLOWS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Resident onboarding\\\\n   a. User visits /register/; enters data + HOA access code.\\\\n   b. Admin receives email “User Registration Requires Approval”.\\\\n   c. Admin logs in → User Registration ▸ Users → Approve.\\\\n   d. User receives “Your account is approved” email, logs in, sees protected menu items.\\\\n\\\\n2. HOA Admin uploads protected PDF (e.g., Annual Meeting Minutes)\\\\n   a. Media ▸ Add New → upload PDF → click “Protect this file”.\\\\n   b. Copy auto-generated shortcode.\\\\n   c. Edit “Annual Meetings” page (block editor) → add ‘Shortcode’ block → paste.\\\\n   d. Click Update; file now downloadable only by Residents.\\\\n\\\\n3. Post News item\\\\n   a. Posts ▸ Add New → title + content; set Category = “Members Only News”.\\\\n   b. Content Control rule can also blanket-protect this category if preferred (create Rule 3 referencing category).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nF. SECURITY / PRIVACY CHECKLIST\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n✔ SSL mandatory.\\\\n✔ Limit Login Attempts active.\\\\n✔ reCAPTCHA on Contact form.\\\\n✔ Manual approval prevents spam users.\\\\n✔ Only essential PII collected (name, email, HOA access code). No DOB, phone, etc.\\\\n✔ Weekly automated backups via host or UpdraftPlus (free) – schedule to external storage (Google Drive free tier).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nG. DESIGN TEAM HOOKS & NOTES\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Theme must output `wp_nav_menu()` location “primary”.\\\\n2. Register sidebar “Protected Sidebar” (optional) if theme offers sidebars → may hold quick-links visible only to Residents via `is_user_logged_in()`.\\\\n3. Ensure CSS for `.pda-protected` shortcode wrapper inherits theme typography.\\\\n4. If using Astra, keep header builder; add custom menu item CSS class `menu-item-protected` (style to match but hide via `display:none` unauth if plugin flashes). Not needed for FSE theme.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nH. DELIVERABLE SUMMARY\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• Working WordPress site with defined IA, plugins configured, roles created.\\\\n• No paid licenses required; all plugins on WP.org repo.\\\\n• Non-technical HOA admins can manage protected documents and news via Gutenberg + Kadence Blocks.\\\\n• Security hardening & privacy minimal compliance done.\\\\n\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_PLAN_V1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CMS_ADJ_V1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Motti (3) with sequence ID CMS_ADJ_V1:\\\\n\\\\n]User decisions for incorporation:\\\\n• Hosting: AWS Lightsail.\\\\n• Contact email: board@dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\n• User will supply a neighborhood hero image later; use a royalty-free placeholder meanwhile.\\\\nTASKS:\\\\n1. Produce an UPDATED DEP (CMS_ADJ_V1) reflecting these items.\\\\n   a. Set WPForms notification destination to board@dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\n   b. Include a short, deterministic instruction for the HOA admin to replace the placeholder hero image once they upload their photo (Gutenberg: replace image block, recommended size 1920×800 px, compress ≤400 KB).\\\\n   c. Confirm the self-registration access code value you will pre-configure (suggest “NEIGHBOR2024” unless you choose differently—state it explicitly).\\\\n2. List any CLI ‘wp-cli’ commands or GUI paths that need environment URLs/IPs supplied by Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the adjusted DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_ADJ_V1.\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_ADJ_V1###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CMS_ADJ_V1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"**UPDATED DEP – CMS_ADJ_V1 (incorporating AWS Lightsail, official board email, hero-image placeholder, and finalized access code)**\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nA. HOSTING ON AWS LIGHTSAIL (Infrastructure)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Create Lightsail instance\\\\n   • Blueprint: *WordPress 6.x* (Ubuntu 22.04 LTS).\\\\n   • Size: *Linux/Unix 1 vCPU, 2 GB RAM* (burstable) – adequate for ≤500 residents.\\\\n   • Allocate static IP → attach to instance.\\\\n   • In Networking tab, add HTTPS (443) to firewall.\\\\n\\\\n2. Domain mapping (when DNS ready)\\\\n   • Point A-record `@` → Static IP, CNAME `www` → `@`.\\\\n   • In Lightsail > Networking > Certificates create Let’s Encrypt certificate for `dunbaroakshoa.com` + `www`. Attach to Load Balancer **or** enable Bitnami HTTPS configuration tool (Bncert) inside instance:  \\\\n     `sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool`\\\\n\\\\n3. System packages (SSH into instance)\\\\n   ```bash\\\\n   sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get upgrade -y\\\\n   sudo ufw disable   # Lightsail firewall already in place\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n4. SMTP (transactional mail)\\\\n   • Use AWS SES *or* free SendGrid. Infrastructure will supply SMTP host, port, user, pass for WP SMTP plugin (already in Bitnami stack).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nB. WORDPRESS BASELINE ADJUSTMENTS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• All prior IA, plugin list, and role definitions remain the same **except**:\\\\n  – WPForms → Notification email now **board@dunbaroakshoa.com**.\\\\n  – Hero image placeholder inserted on Home page (details §D3).\\\\n  – Access Code pre-configured as **NEIGHBOR2024**.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nC. ENV-DEPENDENT CLI COMMANDS / PATHS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nThe following `wp-cli` commands require values supplied by Infrastructure at runtime:\\\\n1. Set Site URL / Home URL (post-DNS):  \\\\n   `wp option update siteurl 'https://dunbaroakshoa.com'`  \\\\n   `wp option update home    'https://dunbaroakshoa.com'`\\\\n2. Update admin email (optional):  \\\\n   `wp option update admin_email 'board@dunbaroakshoa.com'`\\\\n3. Map domain in Bitnami:  \\\\n   `sudo /opt/bitnami/configure_app_domain --domain dunbaroakshoa.com`\\\\n4. Issue SSL via bncert (placeholder prompts for DOMAIN(s) & EMAIL address).\\\\n\\\\nGUI paths requiring URL/IP knowledge:\\\\n• Lightsail → Networking → DNS Zones (enter apex domain, static IP).  \\\\n• WP Admin → Settings ▸ General (Site Address) – pre-filled by blueprint but verify.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD. DETERMINISTIC CONFIGURATION CHANGES\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD1. WPForms (Contact Form)\\\\n   • WPForms ▸ *HOA Contact* ▸ Settings ▸ Notifications  \\\\n     – *Send To Email Address* → `board@dunbaroakshoa.com` (single line).  \\\\n     – Confirm hCaptcha/reCAPTCHA still enabled.\\\\n\\\\nD2. User Registration (Access Code)\\\\n   • Field `hoa_access_code` default validation rule: must equal **“NEIGHBOR2024”** (case-sensitive).  \\\\n   • Display error “Invalid HOA code” on mismatch.\\\\n\\\\nD3. Home Page hero image placeholder & replacement instructions\\\\n   1. Edit *Home* page with Gutenberg.\\\\n   2. Insert *Cover* block at top if not present.  \\\\n      – Upload royalty-free placeholder (e.g., `https://source.unsplash.com/1920x800/?suburb`).  \\\\n      – Block settings: *Fixed background* OFF, *Overlay opacity* 40 %, *Min-height* 800 px.\\\\n   3. HOW HOA ADMIN REPLACES LATER (instruction visible in editor notes):\\\\n      • Click Cover block → Toolbar > Replace > Upload → select new hero image (recommended **1920×800 px, ≤400 KB**, JPEG compressed via tinyjpg.com).  \\\\n      • Update page.  \\\\n   (Design director may add `<!-- TODO: replace-hero-image -->` HTML comment for clarity.)\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nE. QUICK REFERENCE – WORKFLOWS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• Workflows from original DEP stay identical; only contact email and hero image differ.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nF. SECURITY & BACKUPS (NO CHANGE)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• Lightsail snapshots scheduled nightly (retain 7 days).  \\\\n• UpdraftPlus optional – send to Amazon S3 (Lightsail object storage) or Google Drive.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nG. COMPLETION CRITERIA\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. AWS Lightsail instance online at `https://dunbaroakshoa.com` with valid SSL.\\\\n2. Contact form successfully emails `board@dunbaroakshoa.com` (test after SMTP configured).\\\\n3. Resident registration form live at `/register/`, requiring access code **NEIGHBOR2024** and manual admin approval.\\\\n4. Placeholder hero image visible; instruction present in editor comment for easy swap.\\\\n5. All protected pages inaccessible to anonymous visitors.\\\\n\\\\nEND UPDATED DEP\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_ADJ_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_ADJ_V1###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":6510,\"outputTokens\":1480,\"totalTokens\":7990},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0mI8vgwa296hiL29fr6U5QqxtPb\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753404042,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###CMS_ADJ_V1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"**UPDATED DEP – CMS_ADJ_V1 (incorporating AWS Lightsail, official board email, hero-image placeholder, and finalized access code)**\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nA. HOSTING ON AWS LIGHTSAIL (Infrastructure)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Create Lightsail instance\\\\n   • Blueprint: *WordPress 6.x* (Ubuntu 22.04 LTS).\\\\n   • Size: *Linux/Unix 1 vCPU, 2 GB RAM* (burstable) – adequate for ≤500 residents.\\\\n   • Allocate static IP → attach to instance.\\\\n   • In Networking tab, add HTTPS (443) to firewall.\\\\n\\\\n2. Domain mapping (when DNS ready)\\\\n   • Point A-record `@` → Static IP, CNAME `www` → `@`.\\\\n   • In Lightsail > Networking > Certificates create Let’s Encrypt certificate for `dunbaroakshoa.com` + `www`. Attach to Load Balancer **or** enable Bitnami HTTPS configuration tool (Bncert) inside instance:  \\\\n     `sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool`\\\\n\\\\n3. System packages (SSH into instance)\\\\n   ```bash\\\\n   sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get upgrade -y\\\\n   sudo ufw disable   # Lightsail firewall already in place\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n4. SMTP (transactional mail)\\\\n   • Use AWS SES *or* free SendGrid. Infrastructure will supply SMTP host, port, user, pass for WP SMTP plugin (already in Bitnami stack).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nB. WORDPRESS BASELINE ADJUSTMENTS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• All prior IA, plugin list, and role definitions remain the same **except**:\\\\n  – WPForms → Notification email now **board@dunbaroakshoa.com**.\\\\n  – Hero image placeholder inserted on Home page (details §D3).\\\\n  – Access Code pre-configured as **NEIGHBOR2024**.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nC. ENV-DEPENDENT CLI COMMANDS / PATHS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nThe following `wp-cli` commands require values supplied by Infrastructure at runtime:\\\\n1. Set Site URL / Home URL (post-DNS):  \\\\n   `wp option update siteurl 'https://dunbaroakshoa.com'`  \\\\n   `wp option update home    'https://dunbaroakshoa.com'`\\\\n2. Update admin email (optional):  \\\\n   `wp option update admin_email 'board@dunbaroakshoa.com'`\\\\n3. Map domain in Bitnami:  \\\\n   `sudo /opt/bitnami/configure_app_domain --domain dunbaroakshoa.com`\\\\n4. Issue SSL via bncert (placeholder prompts for DOMAIN(s) & EMAIL address).\\\\n\\\\nGUI paths requiring URL/IP knowledge:\\\\n• Lightsail → Networking → DNS Zones (enter apex domain, static IP).  \\\\n• WP Admin → Settings ▸ General (Site Address) – pre-filled by blueprint but verify.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD. DETERMINISTIC CONFIGURATION CHANGES\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD1. WPForms (Contact Form)\\\\n   • WPForms ▸ *HOA Contact* ▸ Settings ▸ Notifications  \\\\n     – *Send To Email Address* → `board@dunbaroakshoa.com` (single line).  \\\\n     – Confirm hCaptcha/reCAPTCHA still enabled.\\\\n\\\\nD2. User Registration (Access Code)\\\\n   • Field `hoa_access_code` default validation rule: must equal **“NEIGHBOR2024”** (case-sensitive).  \\\\n   • Display error “Invalid HOA code” on mismatch.\\\\n\\\\nD3. Home Page hero image placeholder & replacement instructions\\\\n   1. Edit *Home* page with Gutenberg.\\\\n   2. Insert *Cover* block at top if not present.  \\\\n      – Upload royalty-free placeholder (e.g., `https://source.unsplash.com/1920x800/?suburb`).  \\\\n      – Block settings: *Fixed background* OFF, *Overlay opacity* 40 %, *Min-height* 800 px.\\\\n   3. HOW HOA ADMIN REPLACES LATER (instruction visible in editor notes):\\\\n      • Click Cover block → Toolbar > Replace > Upload → select new hero image (recommended **1920×800 px, ≤400 KB**, JPEG compressed via tinyjpg.com).  \\\\n      • Update page.  \\\\n   (Design director may add `<!-- TODO: replace-hero-image -->` HTML comment for clarity.)\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nE. QUICK REFERENCE – WORKFLOWS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• Workflows from original DEP stay identical; only contact email and hero image differ.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nF. SECURITY & BACKUPS (NO CHANGE)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• Lightsail snapshots scheduled nightly (retain 7 days).  \\\\n• UpdraftPlus optional – send to Amazon S3 (Lightsail object storage) or Google Drive.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nG. COMPLETION CRITERIA\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. AWS Lightsail instance online at `https://dunbaroakshoa.com` with valid SSL.\\\\n2. Contact form successfully emails `board@dunbaroakshoa.com` (test after SMTP configured).\\\\n3. Resident registration form live at `/register/`, requiring access code **NEIGHBOR2024** and manual admin approval.\\\\n4. Placeholder hero image visible; instruction present in editor comment for easy swap.\\\\n5. All protected pages inaccessible to anonymous visitors.\\\\n\\\\nEND UPDATED DEP\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_ADJ_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_ADJ_V1###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":6510,\"completion_tokens\":1480,\"total_tokens\":7990,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":3968,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":192,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Director-rank agent, the second-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Director-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Supervisor-rank agents, who themselves are fairly high-level actors who manage other agents. You are responsible for overseeing major operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to the Chief-rank agent, who is the highest authority in the firm.\\n\\nAs a #2 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Supervisor-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Director, all of your recruitments are Supervisor-rank agents. These are fairly high-level agents who will recruit other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" and middle managers down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\\n\\n---ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS FROM YOUR SUPERIOR---\\nYou will design the WordPress information architecture, choose plugins (login, membership, contact form), define user roles, and produce a deterministic plan for implementing pages and protected sections.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CMS_PLAN_V1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Motti (3) with sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1:\\\\n\\\\n]Please draft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for CMS Implementation. Your DEP should:\\\\n1. Define the WordPress information architecture: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected), News & Events (protected).\\\\n2. Recommend and justify specific free/low-cost plugins for: a) resident self-registration (~100 users) with admin approval code; b) content protection/membership; c) simple page builder or block pattern for non-technical updates; d) contact form; e) PDF file management.\\\\n3. Outline exact configuration steps for each plugin, user-role definitions, and sample workflow for the HOA admin to upload/update protected content and news posts without coding.\\\\n4. Address basic security (CAPTCHA, limited login attempts) and privacy (no unnecessary data collection).\\\\n5. List any settings or theme hooks the Design director must accommodate and any hosting prerequisites from Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_PLAN_V1.\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_PLAN_V1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CMS_PLAN_V1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"**Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – CMS_PLAN_V1**\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nA. HOSTING & BASELINE\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Hosting prerequisites (Infrastructure team)\\\\n   a. PHP ≥ 8.1, memory_limit ≥ 256 M, max_upload_filesize ≥ 32 M.\\\\n   b. MariaDB 10.5 / MySQL 8.0, InnoDB default.\\\\n   c. HTTPS enabled (Let’s Encrypt or other TLS cert) before public launch.\\\\n   d. Cron jobs allowed (for WP‐Cron replacement if traffic < 1k/day this can stay virtual).\\\\n   e. SMTP credentials or transactional-mail service (Postmark / SendGrid free tier) for registration emails.\\\\n   f. File-system write permissions for wp-content and install zip uploads.\\\\n\\\\n2. Fresh WordPress 6.5.x install in root directory; enforce automatic minor/major core updates:\\\\n   wp-config.php →\\\\n   define('WP_AUTO_UPDATE_CORE','minor');\\\\n\\\\n3. Theme baseline picked by Design director: “Twenty Twenty-Four” **or** “Astra Free”.\\\\n   • Must support: full-site-editing (FSE) hooks `header`, `footer`, `sidebar` if Astra.\\\\n   • Keep child-theme blank (style.css, functions.php) reserved for any CSS/JS overrides but *initially empty* to keep DEP deterministic.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nB. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE (IA)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nCreate pages in this exact slug order:\\\\n1. `/`  → “Home”\\\\n2. `/contact-us/` → “Contact Us”\\\\n3. `/bylaws/` → “HOA Bylaws” (public)\\\\n4. `/schools/` → “Nearby Schools” (public)\\\\n5. `/dues/` → “Dues” (PROTECTED)\\\\n6. `/annual-meetings/` → “Annual Meetings” (PROTECTED)\\\\n7. `/news-events/` → “News & Events” (PROTECTED)\\\\n\\\\nNavigation menu “Main Menu” created and assigned to Theme primary location using identical order.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nC. PLUGIN STACK (all free unless noted)\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. User self-registration + manual admin approval + access-code field\\\\n   • Plugin: **“User Registration – Custom Registration Form, Login and User Profile”** by WP Everest.\\\\n     – Free tier supports manual approval, custom fields & form shortcodes.\\\\n\\\\n2. Content/membership protection\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Content Control – User Access Restriction”** by Code Atlantic (100 % free, no paywall).\\\\n\\\\n3. Simple page/block builder for non-technical updates\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Kadence Blocks – Gutenberg Blocks for Page Builder Features”** (free) – adds pre-made block patterns, accordions, tabs; stays inside core editor.\\\\n\\\\n4. Contact form with CAPTCHA\\\\n   • Plugin: **“WPForms Lite”** (free) – includes hCaptcha & reCAPTCHA v2/v3 support.\\\\n\\\\n5. PDF file management / embed & protection\\\\n   • Plugin: **“EmbedPress”** (free) – Gutenberg block to embed PDF inline.\\\\n   • **“Prevent Direct Access – PDA Lite”** (free) – protects PDFs so file URLs respect membership rules.\\\\n\\\\n6. Security hardening\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Limit Login Attempts Reloaded”** (free).\\\\n   • (Optional) “WP 2FA” free module if MFA desired later.\\\\n\\\\n7. Role/Capability management convenience\\\\n   • Plugin: **“Members”** by MemberPress (free) – create Custom Role “Resident”.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD. STEP-BY-STEP CONFIGURATION\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nD1. Global order of operations (deterministic):\\\\n   1. Complete WP install (A2).\\\\n   2. Install theme (A3).\\\\n   3. Install *all* plugins in section C but keep them **deactivated**.\\\\n   4. Activate plugins sequentially in this exact order to avoid capability conflicts:\\\\n      a. Members\\\\n      b. User Registration\\\\n      c. Content Control\\\\n      d. Kadence Blocks\\\\n      e. WPForms Lite\\\\n      f. EmbedPress\\\\n      g. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite\\\\n      h. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\n   5. Create roles, forms, rules as below.\\\\n\\\\nD2. Members plugin – role definitions\\\\n   • Create custom role **Resident**.\\\\n     Capabilities: `read`, `edit_posts` = false, `upload_files` = false. (Leave all others unchecked.)\\\\n   • (Core) Keep Administrator, Editor defaults.\\\\n\\\\nD3. User Registration plugin – registration form\\\\n   1. Create new form “Resident Signup”.\\\\n   2. Add core fields: First Name, Last Name, Email (username), Password.\\\\n   3. Add custom Text field “Access Code”.\\\\n      – Field meta-key: `hoa_access_code`.\\\\n      – Field set as *required*.\\\\n   4. Enable *Manual Admin Approval* (Settings ▸ General ▸ User Login Option ▸ “Admin Approve”).\\\\n   5. Form setting ▸ *Enable email confirmation* = OFF (because approval already required).\\\\n   6. Place validation rule via form *Field Visibility & Logic*:\\\\n      – If `hoa_access_code` ≠ “NEIGHBOR2024” (example), display error “Invalid HOA code”.\\\\n   7. Save form; copy generated shortcode `[user_registration_form id=\\\\\\\"XX\\\\\\\"]`.\\\\n   8. Create WordPress page `/register/` titled “Resident Registration”, paste shortcode.\\\\n   9. In WP ▸ Settings ▸ General ▸ “Membership – Anyone can register” = **unchecked** (security).\\\\n\\\\nD4. Content Control – protection rules\\\\n   • Rule 1: Protect Pages `Dues`, `Annual Meetings`, `News & Events`.\\\\n     – Access condition: Logged-in users with role = Resident OR ≥ Editor.\\\\n     – Redirect on failure: `/register/` (or custom message page).\\\\n   • Rule 2: Protect Media Files category “Protected PDFs” (auto-created by PDA Lite) with same role condition.\\\\n\\\\nD5. Prevent Direct Access (PDA) Lite – PDF handling\\\\n   1. Settings ▸ Permalink Type: “Encrypted URL” (default).\\\\n   2. Upload PDF → Media Library → toggle “Protect this file”.\\\\n   3. Copy shortcode `[pda_protected url=\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\" download=\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"]` and insert inside protected pages.\\\\n\\\\nD6. WPForms Lite – contact form\\\\n   1. Create form “HOA Contact”. Fields: Name, Email, Message.\\\\n   2. Settings ▸ Spam Protection → enable Google reCAPTCHA v3 (site key provided separately by Infrastructure).\\\\n   3. Notifications → send to `hoaboard@example.com`.\\\\n   4. Embed form in “Contact Us” page using Gutenberg block.\\\\n\\\\nD7. Limit Login Attempts Reloaded\\\\n   • Settings → Lockout at 4 retries, 30 min lockout, 24 h increase, GDPR consent banner OFF.\\\\n\\\\nD8. Kadence Blocks (non-technical editing enablement)\\\\n   • Install Starter Templates if Astra theme chosen; else use built-in patterns.\\\\n   • Provide training doc (outside DEP) listing: Accordion (meeting minutes), Info Box (dues summary), Gallery (events photos).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nE. SAMPLE WORKFLOWS\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Resident onboarding\\\\n   a. User visits /register/; enters data + HOA access code.\\\\n   b. Admin receives email “User Registration Requires Approval”.\\\\n   c. Admin logs in → User Registration ▸ Users → Approve.\\\\n   d. User receives “Your account is approved” email, logs in, sees protected menu items.\\\\n\\\\n2. HOA Admin uploads protected PDF (e.g., Annual Meeting Minutes)\\\\n   a. Media ▸ Add New → upload PDF → click “Protect this file”.\\\\n   b. Copy auto-generated shortcode.\\\\n   c. Edit “Annual Meetings” page (block editor) → add ‘Shortcode’ block → paste.\\\\n   d. Click Update; file now downloadable only by Residents.\\\\n\\\\n3. Post News item\\\\n   a. Posts ▸ Add New → title + content; set Category = “Members Only News”.\\\\n   b. Content Control rule can also blanket-protect this category if preferred (create Rule 3 referencing category).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nF. SECURITY / PRIVACY CHECKLIST\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n✔ SSL mandatory.\\\\n✔ Limit Login Attempts active.\\\\n✔ reCAPTCHA on Contact form.\\\\n✔ Manual approval prevents spam users.\\\\n✔ Only essential PII collected (name, email, HOA access code). No DOB, phone, etc.\\\\n✔ Weekly automated backups via host or UpdraftPlus (free) – schedule to external storage (Google Drive free tier).\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nG. DESIGN TEAM HOOKS & NOTES\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n1. Theme must output `wp_nav_menu()` location “primary”.\\\\n2. Register sidebar “Protected Sidebar” (optional) if theme offers sidebars → may hold quick-links visible only to Residents via `is_user_logged_in()`.\\\\n3. Ensure CSS for `.pda-protected` shortcode wrapper inherits theme typography.\\\\n4. If using Astra, keep header builder; add custom menu item CSS class `menu-item-protected` (style to match but hide via `display:none` unauth if plugin flashes). Not needed for FSE theme.\\\\n\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nH. DELIVERABLE SUMMARY\\\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n• Working WordPress site with defined IA, plugins configured, roles created.\\\\n• No paid licenses required; all plugins on WP.org repo.\\\\n• Non-technical HOA admins can manage protected documents and news via Gutenberg + Kadence Blocks.\\\\n• Security hardening & privacy minimal compliance done.\\\\n\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CMS_PLAN_V1\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_PLAN_V1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CMS_ADJ_V1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Motti (3) with sequence ID CMS_ADJ_V1:\\\\n\\\\n]User decisions for incorporation:\\\\n• Hosting: AWS Lightsail.\\\\n• Contact email: board@dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\n• User will supply a neighborhood hero image later; use a royalty-free placeholder meanwhile.\\\\nTASKS:\\\\n1. Produce an UPDATED DEP (CMS_ADJ_V1) reflecting these items.\\\\n   a. Set WPForms notification destination to board@dunbaroakshoa.com.\\\\n   b. Include a short, deterministic instruction for the HOA admin to replace the placeholder hero image once they upload their photo (Gutenberg: replace image block, recommended size 1920×800 px, compress ≤400 KB).\\\\n   c. Confirm the self-registration access code value you will pre-configure (suggest “NEIGHBOR2024” unless you choose differently—state it explicitly).\\\\n2. List any CLI ‘wp-cli’ commands or GUI paths that need environment URLs/IPs supplied by Infrastructure.\\\\nReturn the adjusted DEP in your Report for sequence ID CMS_ADJ_V1.\\\"\\n}\\n###CMS_ADJ_V1###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1753404042275,"endTime":1753404088965.411}